{"filePath":"/home/john/.claude/projects/-home-john-mynotes/memory/project_defect_cocycle_csuite.md","newString":"**PROOF PHASE (critiques/dc_proofs.md wish list; its Phase-1 item 1 DONE).** Proved in finite_spectral_shadows.tex (11pp): **(1) Coboundary classification Cob=⟨χ₂⟩** on sync residue×parity, arbitrary weights/tilt, λ-twisted form included — proof compares branches b,b+2 (2 primitive root ⇒ d is squares-invariant ⇒ d=D(χ₂(a),τ); then cocycle+key identity ⇒ χ trivial on squares); bypasses the 3-adic-log route. **(2) Strict gap every level** (L₁ primitive + Wielandt equality ⇒ classification). **(3) Conductor collapse**: spec(L^(r)_χ)\\{0}=spec(L^(c)_χ)\\{0} via character filtration (η∘A drops conductor; quotient nilpotent) ⇒ κ_{3^r}=1−max_{c≤r}γ_c, γ_c r-independent (confirmed EXACTLY). **(4) Strip rotation identity** L_{χ₂}=e^{−iπc*/R}DL₁D⁻¹ (commutes with truncation). NUMERICS: γ_c^par through c=6 — s0: .6547 .7638 .7629 .7202 .7147; s1: .9078 .8691 .9264 .9210 .9021 — bounded, peaks at FIXED conductor; **monotonicity FALSE for bare operator** (γ₄>γ₂ @s1), true for killed strip s0. Functional eq ψ(3a+1)=λψ(a)χ(a): only (1,1),(χ₂,χ₂) for r≤4. Remaining: single Conjecture (bounded-conductor extremality sup_c γ_c<1) ⇒ conditional constant gap (κ₀^par=0.2362 s0/0.0736 s1; strip 0.0931); open strip non-product-form classification; then wish-list #3 cancellation, #5 height transfer, #1 keystone.\n\n**aipm:** 18 captures + 1 run event; `ailog validate` passes. NOT git-committed (mynotes has many unrelated pending changes — leave commit to user).","oldString":"**aipm:** 17 captures + 1 run event; `ailog validate` passes. NOT git-committed (mynotes has many unrelated pending changes — leave commit to user).","originalFile":"---\nname: project-defect-cocycle-csuite\ndescription: Collatz deterministic defect cocycle — C numerical suite build (Experiments A–I) + aipm provenance\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3d506146-0c9f-463a-a710-cacb38cea0a3\n---\n\nBuilding the C numerical test suite specified in `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/collatz_defect_cocycle_c_specs.tex`, testing the defect cocycle W_{n,ℓ}(x;χ,s) of `defect_cocycle.tex`. Goal: is the finite spectral-shadow principle numerically plausible — NOT to prove Collatz. Critique read at `critiques/dc_1.md`.\n\n- **Code:** `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/c_suite/`, executable `collatz_tests`, 9 subcommands (A–I). ISO C11; `make` (FAST128 default), `make GMP=1`, `make DEBUG=1`; `make test` runs unit checks. Part of the `mynotes` git repo (not its own).\n- **aipm:** `.aipm/` initialized here (profile experimental-science, manuscript defect_cocycle.tex); claude-code capture hooks installed to project `.claude/settings.json`; added `**/*.c`,`**/*.h` to scan globs. Use installed `ailog` 0.1.0 (pipx, on PATH) — **lacks `prereg`/`graph`** (canonical repo f49bf3d has them; installed from 6f8a4ca). Pre-registrations logged via `ailog add`. Wrap builds/runs in `ailog run --`.\n\n**Critique-driven requirements baked in:** (1) Exp H mod-3^r congruence is a correctness GATE built first; (2) report rho_annealed and rho_exact as SEPARATE columns (never substitute annealed Fourier for exact operator); (3) shadow search flags limsup plateaus AND long sparse blocks, not just positive-density; (4) quenched pressure = limsup (1/n)Σ sΔ_b, not sum-over-words.\n\n**Progress: ALL 9 EXPERIMENTS BUILT & VALIDATED (M0–M4 done).** README.md + VALIDATION_REPORT.md written. Builds clean FAST128/GMP/DEBUG; `make test` passes.\n- **M0.** collatz_core/bigval (FAST128+GMP), orbit_scan, modarith, io_csv, config, main. Exp H GATE PASSES: 226128/226128 (seeds 3–9999, r≤8) + 144/144 GMP (seed 9999999999999999, r=12, deep n) → mod-3^r identity confirmed.\n- **M1.** entropy_stats, critical_events. (A) height tail slope ≈ −1. (B) boundary-excluded middle bulk leans to p^(1) (KL_to_p1<KL_to_annealed).\n- **M2.** characters (additive + mult-3^r), defect_sums (W via complex prefix), per-step residue capture, segment labeler. (C) |W|@s=0 decays with window len. (D) post-exit taboo: KL_to_p=0.18 ≪ KL_to_p1=0.57, M_post(1)≈0.99<1.\n- **M3.** sparse_matrix (CSR, power iteration), residue_height_graph (forward map Q odd, inverse branch Q⊥3, killed height band). (E) nontrivial sectors strictly below trivial; s=1 k=1 smallest gap 0.994. (F) exact gap DEVIATES from annealed |p̂| by ±0.1–0.36 (separate columns; finiteness leak real).\n- **M4.** Exp G (dense tr(L^n)+det(1-zL) via LU). Exp I (shadow-search): raw δ=0.1 saturates (short windows+max-over-grid) → added length-scaled null, require ≥3×. Then 4.8% flag; critical_C_A 8.3%>high_ascent 5.8%>post_exit 3.7%; shadow rate grows with len → 97.8% @len64+ (n=44, caveat). Single-orbit |W| noise-dominated short; clean signal is operator gap (E/F).\n\n**LARGE-SCALE RUN done** (out_large/, `run_large.sh`, FAST128 release; raw CSVs gitignored, big ones gzipped, ~270M). Regenerated VALIDATION_REPORT.md. Headlines: H 23.9M/23.9M pass; A slope −0.97 (oct 10–28); B oct26 103976 middle segs KL→p¹ 0.093 ≪ KL→ann 0.191 (decisive Cramér); D KL→p 0.177 ≪ KL→p¹ 0.576; **E κ_Q bounded 0.09–0.42, does NOT shrink as Q→243 (supports uniform-gap κ_Q≳1/polylog Q)**; **F corr(exact,annealed)=0.38, mean|dev|=0.254 → exact gap ≠ annealed Fourier shadow (finiteness leak real)**; I 1.25M windows 4.2% shadow, critical 8.4%>high 5.4%>post-exit 3.2%, shadow rate→100% at len64+ (n=218).\n\n**I↔E/F RELATION done** (SHADOW_OPERATOR_RELATION.md). Found: **E killed-height power iteration does NOT converge** (residuals 3–9%, hit MAXIT; height-transport band → near-degenerate top eigenvalues; some gap_ratio>1 violating Wielandt) → E's κ_Q unreliable, needs Arnoldi/shift-invert; **use residue-only F** (all ratios <1, converges; fixed F baseline to principal-on-units mult k=0). Relation: shadows concentrate at the weakest-gap tilt (82% of 53158, 100% of 218 long shadows at s=1; F s=1 gaps weaker than s=0); long shadows in weaker-gap sectors (0.73 vs 0.57) — predicted direction. BUT per-sector confounded: 94% of shadows at smallest Q=9 (finite-class inflation), corr(|W|,gap)=+0.25 only → single-orbit shadow tracks residue-class count not gap (circularity leak made concrete; F shows no anti-gap). TODO: harden E solver; make Exp C use mult chars for 3^r; normalize shadow detector by residue-class count.\n\n**E SOLVER HARDENED (Arnoldi).** Implemented complex Givens + Hessenberg single-shift QR eigensolver (Wilkinson shift+deflation) + restarted complex Arnoldi (MGS+reorth, Krylov 40→240) in sparse_matrix.c as `csr_spectral_radius_arnoldi`; unit-tested vs known spectra (real/complex diag, cyclic perm roots-of-unity, power-iter agreement). Wired into Exp E & F. RESULT: killed-height op now converges residual <8e-11, ZERO Wielandt violations (was 3–9%, gap_ratio>1). Reliable κ_Q (min over first 4 mult chars): Q=9 0.093, 27 0.190, 81 0.306, 243 0.329 — GROWS with Q, bounded from 0, TILT-INDEPENDENT (earlier s-dependence was nonconvergence). Target 1 now Confirmed in the .tex (10pp). Shadow↔F relation unchanged (corr +0.25, long gap 0.73 vs 0.57). Remaining: κ_Q over full char group + larger Q for the Q→∞ finiteness leak.\n\n**FULL-GROUP κ_Q + higher Q (Q→3⁷=2187).** Added `--char-cap 0` = full character group (conj symmetry k=1..φ/2) to Exp E/F. **MAJOR CORRECTION:** uniform gap = 1−**MAX**_χ ratio (worst char); prior turn's \"κ_Q grows 0.093→0.329\" used 1−min (best char) over 4 chars — wrong, retracted. CORRECTED (Arnoldi, residuals~0): **killed-height κ_Q=0 at every Q** — quadratic char k=φ/2 has ρ(L_χ)=ρ(L_0) exactly (=residue-independent height-transport eigenvalue 0.9119@s0, Q-independent); artifact of height appended uncoupled from char. **Residue-only κ_Q STABILIZES** (s=0→0.236, s=1→0.074, Q=27..2187), bounded from 0, worst char at FIXED freq (not k=1); exact op gaps low-freq k=1 by 0.24–0.78 vs annealed→0 ⇒ **annealed finiteness leak REFUTED for residue operator**. Docs updated (VALIDATION_REPORT, SHADOW_OPERATOR_RELATION, .tex 10pp: residue-only Target1 Confirmed, killed-height Flagged). Open: rebuild height coordinate COUPLED to character to remove the quadratic artifact. Big outputs in out_kappa/ (gitignored).\n\n**HEIGHT COUPLED TO CHARACTER (Exp E `--height-mode {sync|factored}`).** Diagnostic: the killed-height quadratic-char degeneracy (ρ(L_χ)=ρ(L_0)) is STRUCTURAL — exactly 1.0 across R∈{2..16}, L∈{24..120}. Mechanism: height≈n·log₂3−Bₙ encodes Bₙ; quadratic char's χ(2)⁻ᵇ=(−1)ᵇ → (−1)^{Bₙ}, a coboundary of the skew product (removable for any height geometry). FIX: `factored` = L_res(χ)⊗T_height (height = residue-independent survival factor). Result: quadratic char gapped (0.333 s0/0.600 s1 = residue value); uniform κ_Q = residue gap exactly (0.345 Q9→0.236 Q≥27 @s0; 0.092→0.074 @s1), matches F; Kronecker factor cancels → holds all Q. Killed op now inherits the stabilizing residue gap + gaps every char. Added rhg_build height_mode param; .tex Target1 killed-height = Resolved (10pp). Residual theory Q: prove the (−1)^{Bₙ}↔height coboundary; choose sync-vs-factored as the H23a vehicle.\n\n**QUADRATIC COBOUNDARY PROVED** (Appendix A of defect_cocycle_with_findings.tex, 12pp). Chain: χ₂ factors through mod 3 (=Legendre; ker=squares={u≡1 mod3}); **χ₂(S(x))=(−1)^{v₂(3x+1)}** (via 2≡−1, 3x+1≡1 mod 3); ∏χ₂(xᵢ)=(−1)^{Bₙ}; on skew product residue×(Bₙ mod2), d(a,τ)=χ₂(a)(−1)^τ gives L_{χ₂}=D L₁D⁻¹ → isospectral, κ=0 for any tilt/height-disc. Residue-only ratio exactly (2^{1+s}−1)/(2^{1+s}+1)=1/3(s0)/3/5(s1) from 2-state mod-3 operator (matches F). Only quadratic removable (χ(3a+1) nonconstant for order>2 since 3a+1 is a square) → explains max-ratio=1 only at k=φ/2. Verified numerically (identity 1e5 seeds; direct diag: residue-only 1/3, residue×parity 1.0). The κ_Q=0 is now a theorem, not a flag.\n\n**H23a OPERATOR DECIDED: faithful SYNC skew product, on the coboundary-quotient, relative to the valuation-pushforward (non-uniform) residue reference.** Why: (1) inverse argument needs faithfulness — only sync's ρ governs actual W_n (one b drives residue+height); factored decouples b. (2) factored's χ₂ gap is a MIRAGE — W_n(χ₂,0)→−1/3 (mean −0.353 over 3.2e4 orbits), does NOT decay; sync correctly gives ρ(L_χ₂)=ρ(L₀). (3) χ₂ coboundary ⇒ residues non-uniform mod 3 (1/3:2/3), so χ₂ is part of the reference, not an obstruction; H23a on quotient by coboundaries. (4) there sync has positive Q-uniform gap: worst non-coboundary char ξ=1/6, κ_Q=0.0931 IDENTICAL for Q=9,27,81,243, both tilts, ≳1/polylog. factored/residue-only = diagnostics (pure residue gap (2^{1+s}−1)/(2^{1+s}+1)=0.236/0.074). Doc: .tex §\"Which operator powers H23a\" (13pp) + VALIDATION_REPORT. OPEN: prove κ_Q≳1/polylog for sync on coboundary-quotient at all Q.\n\n**dc_3.md critique incorporated (manuscript now 15pp).** H23a REFORMULATED: gap for all NON-COBOUNDARY characters (not all nontrivial); χ₂ is part of the valuation reference. New Appendix B \"sync quotient gap, by conductor\": **κ_Q is CONSTANT κ₀≈0.0931, not just polylog** — each conductor-3ᶜ char's gap is r-independent (PROVED: mod-3ᶜ reduction autonomous since (3a+1) mod 3ᶜ depends only on a mod 3^{c-1}); gap ratio by conductor (r-indep): 3=1.0(cob),9=0.9069,27=0.8530,81=0.8261,243=0.7306; worst = fixed conductor-9 (order-6) → κ₀ constant; higher conductors strictly more gapped. Lemma (coboundary classification: only ⟨χ₂⟩) + 5-step proof program (complete-fiber principal-unit cancellation is the open input). Verified Q=9,27,81,243. critiques/dc_3.md endorses the sync/coboundary-quotient decision.\n\n**SPLIT INTO PUBLICATION + COMPANION (dc_4.md critique).** Manuscript renamed **\"Finite Spectral Shadows for the Collatz Valuation Cocycle\"** (J.A.Janik). Two docs now: **finite_spectral_shadows.tex** (8pp publication: PartI object+inverse principle, II rigorous identities [sliding-window congruence + quadratic coboundary, both with proofs], III numerical-evidence summary, IV refined H23a target) and **finite_spectral_shadows_computational.tex** (4pp companion: suite, operators+Arnoldi, Exp A–I, shadow↔operator relation). Old defect_cocycle_with_findings.tex SUPERSEDED. dc_4 fixes applied: constant-gap downgraded to Prop(autonomy,proved)+Conj(monotonicity)+Conditional Cor; coboundary classification Prop(forward)+Conj(no further); source-twist Convention explicit; Ω_Q→U_{3^r} multiplicative; critical_C_A/high_ascent/post_exit marked EXPLORATORY; inverse principle no longer overconcludes (→\"no persistent non-coboundary shadow\"). Both compile clean. Critiques so far: dc_1 (defect cocycle), dc_3 (operator decision + conductor), dc_4 (publication split/status).\n\nCompanion now self-contained: VALIDATION_REPORT tables folded into finite_spectral_shadows_computational.tex Appendix A \"Validation data\" (6pp): run-params table, Exp B bulk table, residue-only κ_Q-vs-Q + sync-by-conductor tables, Exp I by-label/by-length + shadow↔operator join. Used corrected uniform-gap (1−max) numbers; retracted 1−min E table explicitly superseded.\n\n**aipm:** 17 captures + 1 run event; `ailog validate` passes. NOT git-committed (mynotes has many unrelated pending changes — leave commit to user).\n\n**OPEN — needs user decision:** the \"C_A-critical\" definition is project-internal (H23a/PVT/SRCE, carried over without restatement). The spec's literal `V^2 ≤ 2^A P` floods event counts (every excursion once the orbit descends to small record-low V). Added `--crit-mode {vsq|height}`; `height` (peak ≥ launch·2^A) is the cleaner \"high ascent\" reading. Both show the Cramér-tilt direction in the middle bulk. Affects Exp B/D and the critical/high_ascent segment labels in C/I — confirm the formal certificate before finalizing those. Related to [[project-aipm]] dogfooding (installed CLI missing prereg/graph).\n","replaceAll":false,"structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" "," Companion now self-contained: VALIDATION_REPORT tables folded into finite_spectral_shadows_computational.tex Appendix